{#- B-2 coverage statement: one per run (worked example, section 4). As long
    as the facts require: completion, evidence, images and thermal, sensor
    availability, then the record's own contradictions, in descending order of
    how badly they compromise the record. A paragraph with nothing wrong is one
    sentence; one that has nothing to say is left out.

    Every argument that prints a value is a slot placeholder from
    b2_narrative.Writer; code fills it. Arguments ending in _n are plain numbers
    used only to choose wording, and are never printed. The literal text holds
    no digits and no number words. A line starting "- " is a bullet. -#}

{# --- completion --- #}

{% macro route(required, required_n) -%}
The route defines {{ required }} required checkpoint{{ "" if required_n == 1 else "s" }}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro empty() -%}
No checkpoints were recorded for this run.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro all_completed(completed) -%}
All {{ completed }} were reached and completed, and none were missed.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro completion(completed, required, missed, missed_n) -%}
{{ completed }} of the {{ required }} were completed{% if missed_n %} and {{ missed }} {{ "was" if missed_n == 1 else "were" }} missed:{% else %}.{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro missed_item(name, reason) -%}
- {{ name }}: {% if reason %}"{{ reason }}"{% else %}no reason recorded{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{# --- evidence --- #}

{% macro all_evidence(reached) -%}
All {{ reached }} checkpoints reached captured evidence.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro some_evidence(with_evidence, reached) -%}
{{ with_evidence }} of the {{ reached }} checkpoints reached captured evidence.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro no_evidence_item(bullet, name, observed) -%}
{{ "- " if bullet else "" }}{{ name }} captured none{% if observed %}, and is recorded with observed: {{ observed }}{% endif %}.
{%- endmacro %}

{# --- images and thermal --- #}

{% macro images(with_evidence, with_evidence_n, images, resolved) -%}
Across the {{ with_evidence }} checkpoint{{ "" if with_evidence_n == 1 else "s" }} that captured evidence, {{ images }} images were referenced{% if resolved %} and {{ resolved }} resolved{% endif %}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro thermal_complete() -%}
Each of them captured a thermal image for every direction photographed.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro thermal_lead(word) -%}
Thermal coverage was {{ word }}:
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro thermal_full(names) -%}
- A thermal image for every direction photographed: {{ names }}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro thermal_partial(items) -%}
- Thermal images for some directions: {{ items }}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro thermal_some(name, pairs, directions) -%}
{{ name }} ({{ pairs }} of {{ directions }})
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro thermal_none(names) -%}
- No thermal images: {{ names }}.
{%- endmacro %}

{# --- sensor availability --- #}

{% macro offline(label, device, block, flag, off) -%}
{{ label }} readings were not recorded. The {{ device }} sensor reported {{ flag }}: false at all {{ off }} checkpoints that reported it, so the {{ block }} block is excluded from this report.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro available_everywhere(labels, n) -%}
{{ labels }} readings were available at all {{ n }} checkpoints reached.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro available_some(label, n, reached) -%}
{{ label }} readings were available at {{ n }} of the {{ reached }} checkpoints reached; the others were excluded:
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro excluded_item(reason, count) -%}
- {{ reason }}: {{ count }}
{%- endmacro %}

{# --- the record's own contradictions (moved from the executive summary) --- #}

{% macro conflict_lead() -%}
The record's declared counts disagree with its own data:
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro count_conflict(declared, label, computed, held_in) -%}
- The record declares {{ declared }} {{ label }}; its {{ held_in }} holds {{ computed }}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro warned_conflict(declared, warned, required, alerts, alerts_n, critical) -%}
- The record declares {{ declared }} checkpoints in a warned state. {{ warned }} of the {{ required }} checkpoints carry a WARN result or a sensor warning{% if alerts_n %}, and {{ alerts }} sensor alert{{ "" if alerts_n == 1 else "s" }} {{ "was" if alerts_n == 1 else "were" }} logged during the run, {{ critical }} of them critical{% endif %}.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro unreconciled() -%}
Both figures are reported as recorded. They have not been reconciled.
{%- endmacro %}
